WEBVTT

00:07.520 --> 00:10.610
Koi seyo shounen shoujo tachi

00:11.160 --> 00:14.220
Kirari hitomi ni hoshi irete

00:14.730 --> 00:17.720
Umareta manma no jounetsu ga

00:18.460 --> 00:21.230
Hibana chirasu Jungle Hare nochi Guu!

00:21.830 --> 00:24.890
Mekurumeku koshitsuki MUCHO

00:25.470 --> 00:28.670
Kodomo nya kiwadoi AMIGO

00:29.210 --> 00:32.270
Kisu shitara suikomaresou

00:32.680 --> 00:35.310
Kowai mono mitasa TONIGHT

00:36.250 --> 00:38.350
Ojikeduitara dame

00:38.350 --> 00:40.120
Oshite osarete GOING

00:40.120 --> 00:41.990
Dokkiri kibun ga iine

00:41.990 --> 00:43.590
Chakkari asa made DANCING

00:43.590 --> 00:45.460
LOVE LOVE LOVE

00:45.460 --> 00:48.860
TROPICANA

00:50.630 --> 00:53.860
Yashi no kokage de tsukamaete

00:54.400 --> 00:57.560
Jirashite tokoton tokoton

00:58.070 --> 01:01.200
Gomen ne anata wa mou toriko

01:01.840 --> 01:04.900
Nigerarenai Jungle Hare nochi Guu!

01:05.450 --> 01:08.350
Koi seyo shounen shoujo tachi

01:08.980 --> 01:11.920
Kirari hitomi ni hoshi irete

01:12.590 --> 01:15.550
Umareta manma no jounetsu ga

01:16.360 --> 01:18.150
Hibana chirasu Jungle Hare nochi Guu!

01:22.860 --> 01:24.190
Time to have some!

01:26.060 --> 01:28.120
Oh my, Haré-sama, you shouldn't do that.

01:28.730 --> 01:32.860
It's basic table manners not to make noise
while drinking tea.

01:33.000 --> 01:33.900
Oh, sorry.

01:33.970 --> 01:35.210
That's right.

01:35.210 --> 01:37.730
I've been telling him over and over...

01:38.640 --> 01:41.010
You just don't sound convincing. That's all.

01:41.510 --> 01:43.240
Ah! I see!

01:43.450 --> 01:46.750
Haré-sama, think of this as an opportunity to
learn table manners!

01:46.750 --> 01:49.720
PACHIMON

01:50.090 --> 01:55.420
Now, the manners I'd like you to learn most
are the those for a French meal.

01:55.690 --> 01:57.330
That's right! Do your best!

01:57.330 --> 02:03.400
Bell-sensei, presently I
believe the person who needs to learn
manners the most is close by.

02:03.400 --> 02:04.230
But what do you think?

02:04.700 --> 02:06.040
I wonder who that could be.

02:06.040 --> 02:07.040
It's you!

02:07.040 --> 02:07.900
What?

02:08.170 --> 02:11.770
If it's something this troublesome, I won't do
it unless you show me an example first!

02:12.240 --> 02:13.940
Geez, you take advantage
of things way too much!

02:14.040 --> 02:17.070
To not do it after your son goes that far...

02:19.350 --> 02:21.720
The way you were dressed until a few
minutes ago seems like it was all a lie.

02:22.590 --> 02:24.180
When I put my mind to it, I can do it.

02:24.650 --> 02:27.150
Hey, why do I have to change clothes?

02:27.320 --> 02:29.450
This is to get into the mood.

02:29.690 --> 02:33.860
Now, please believe that where we're headed
is a top-tier restaurant.

02:35.700 --> 02:36.760
W-What is this?

02:37.000 --> 02:37.800
You prepared this?

02:37.870 --> 02:39.530
This looks like a restaurant, right?

02:40.140 --> 02:41.570
And the people?

02:42.240 --> 02:44.330
They are all servants for this house.

02:44.770 --> 02:46.240
Are they all bored?

02:46.580 --> 02:47.510
Welcome.

02:47.610 --> 02:48.710
A party of five?

02:48.710 --> 02:48.980
Yes.

02:48.980 --> 02:50.070
Even Ashio, too?

02:50.280 --> 02:55.240
In any case, Mom is Mom so her fake
demeanor will be revealed soon enough.

02:55.420 --> 02:56.110
Haré!

02:56.320 --> 02:59.910
Just you watch,
how your mother lives her life!

03:00.160 --> 03:01.650
But, it's just table manners, right?

03:12.200 --> 03:14.070
That was a fine meal.

03:14.400 --> 03:16.970
That was perfect, Ojou-sama!

03:16.970 --> 03:18.670
Your voice is so different.

03:18.740 --> 03:19.970
Shut up.

03:20.080 --> 03:22.680
If you keep whining, I'll shut that mouth of
yours for you, brat.

03:22.680 --> 03:24.580
Don't threaten me with
that poised look of yours.

03:25.010 --> 03:26.810
Ah, I'm worn out!

03:26.920 --> 03:29.050
And don't you change right back!

03:29.050 --> 03:30.350
Another glass of wine!

03:30.420 --> 03:33.820
Wait, Bell, you don't care if the manners are
like some quick trick?

03:34.090 --> 03:35.580
Well, now that you mention it...

03:36.230 --> 03:37.920
Bell, I love you!

03:39.100 --> 03:41.690
It's okay. It's totally okay!

03:41.760 --> 03:42.560
So useless...

03:42.870 --> 03:44.830
Next, it's your turn,
Haré-sama and Guu-sama.

03:44.830 --> 03:47.500
The meal will be arriving soon,
so maintain grace.

03:48.500 --> 03:49.840
Sorry to make you wait!

03:50.710 --> 03:53.900
Sir, is this your first time here?

03:54.410 --> 03:56.400
Weda-san, what's that look?

03:56.850 --> 03:58.400
A cute little waitress!

03:59.250 --> 04:00.610
What are you doing!?

04:01.620 --> 04:03.520
First, how to drink soup...

04:03.590 --> 04:04.480
I guess I'll do it.

04:04.990 --> 04:07.620
Take the spoon, slide it in from the front of
the bowl, and scoop away from you.

04:07.620 --> 04:09.560
Drink the soup by pouring the soup on the
spoon into your mouth from the tip.

04:09.560 --> 04:10.990
Drink the soup by pouring the soup on the
spoon into your mouth from the tip.
See, all gone.

04:10.990 --> 04:11.730
Don't place the spoon perpendicular to your
mouth, or lick the spoon.
Piece of cake, huh?

04:11.730 --> 04:14.360
Don't place the spoon perpendicular to your
mouth, or lick the spoon.
Regardless of how you do it,
don't eat the plate...

04:14.860 --> 04:17.300
You use the outermost knife and fork first.

04:17.830 --> 04:21.240
It takes time to get used to knives and forks,
but for now, try to use them well.

04:21.240 --> 04:23.440
Oh, it's easy to clink them against the plates,
so do be careful of that...

04:23.440 --> 04:24.970
Oh, it's easy to clink them against the plates,
so do be careful of that...
Oh, this is so troublesome!

04:24.970 --> 04:27.780
...and cut the food into portions that are easy
for you to eat, then secure it on the fork.
Mom, do I really have to learn this?

04:27.780 --> 04:28.180
When you bring it close to your mouth, don't
hurry - bring it up slowly. Open your mouth
only a little bit, and bite in.

04:28.180 --> 04:30.980
When you bring it close to your mouth, don't
hurry - bring it up slowly. Open your mouth
only a little bit, and bite in.
Oh, I lack manners, so if you talk to me,
you'll become uncouth, too.

04:30.980 --> 04:33.350
Oh, I lack manners, so if you talk to me,
you'll become uncouth, too.

04:33.520 --> 04:35.610
Now she's all sulking and stuff...

04:36.550 --> 04:38.520
Ah, I'm so tired...

04:38.590 --> 04:39.260
Why is Mom like that?

04:39.260 --> 04:41.420
Why is Weda-san like that?
Why is Mom like that?

04:42.130 --> 04:43.020
You too, Robert?

04:44.030 --> 04:46.790
Oh, pardon me, that was nothing.

04:48.500 --> 04:51.230
But still, you've got one giant sigh there.

04:51.230 --> 04:53.000
Haré-sama, you're so kind.

04:53.240 --> 04:55.140
You're going to listen to my story, huh?

04:55.740 --> 04:57.400
Actually, I don't think I have a choice.

04:57.640 --> 05:01.370
I came to this city after
I graduated from high school.

05:22.670 --> 05:25.930
...and while I didn't know
left from right, Bell-san found me.

05:27.870 --> 05:31.330
She arranged things so that I could work in
this mansion.

05:31.740 --> 05:34.040
I really admire Bell-san.

05:34.640 --> 05:37.740
She's a strong, kind, amazing person!

05:37.980 --> 05:38.640
Really...

05:39.080 --> 05:42.920
That's why when I heard that she was going
to the jungle to pick Weda-san...

05:43.350 --> 05:46.350
What kind of a person is the young lady?

05:46.520 --> 05:49.650
My angel, my dream, my happiness...

05:49.930 --> 05:52.720
Ojou-sama is my everything!

05:54.000 --> 05:55.400
If you fall for her, I'll kill you.

05:55.530 --> 05:56.190
Understood!

05:57.030 --> 05:59.090
I knew her face from photographs...

05:59.300 --> 06:01.240
But since Bell-san was so
head-over-heels for her...

06:01.300 --> 06:07.500
I thought that she must be an innocent,
elegant, beautiful person like a white lily that
just came into bloom.

06:07.940 --> 06:09.210
The exact opposite.

06:09.280 --> 06:10.870
That's right! She's the exact opposite!

06:11.110 --> 06:13.510
I'm sorry, Mom... I can't deny that.

06:13.780 --> 06:14.610
So...

06:14.850 --> 06:16.790
If you talk to me, you'll become uncouth, too.

06:16.790 --> 06:18.120
If you talk to me, you'll become uncouth, too.
Things like that should be...

06:22.160 --> 06:23.460
You shouldn't do that.

06:23.790 --> 06:28.230
If you were to speak with me, your
mannerisms will be lacking as well.

06:28.560 --> 06:30.120
Whose mother is that?

06:30.570 --> 06:32.970
In the first place,
she's so adored by Bell-san...

06:32.970 --> 06:35.530
...and the worst part is that she doesn't
realize it at all!

06:35.610 --> 06:36.830
Poor Bell-san!

06:37.110 --> 06:39.440
Are you in love with Bell?

06:40.180 --> 06:41.670
Oh, no! Of course not.

06:41.780 --> 06:42.640
You're not?

06:43.110 --> 06:44.310
Bell-san is...

06:44.750 --> 06:46.010
...my idol.

06:47.350 --> 06:49.090
She's strong.

06:49.090 --> 06:51.620
She can do anything, and yet she doesn't
forget to do her best...

06:51.620 --> 06:54.490
I wish I could be like that.

06:54.860 --> 06:55.760
That's why...

06:56.030 --> 06:59.130
I want Weda-san to be a person worthy of
being someone that Bell-san...

06:59.130 --> 07:02.290
...whom I look up to so much,
in return looks up to herself.

07:09.710 --> 07:13.470
So Robert doesn't like Mom too much.

07:13.980 --> 07:14.940
More precisely, he hates her?

07:14.940 --> 07:17.350
Can you be a bit less blunt than that?

07:17.350 --> 07:21.280
It can be believed that there
are parts of him that don't exactly hate her,
but to make a final decision...

07:21.280 --> 07:23.480
That's beating around the bush too much!
I don't understand you!

07:24.490 --> 07:25.820
You know, Guu...

07:26.960 --> 07:30.080
I wish Robert would fall in love with Mom.

07:31.430 --> 07:34.460
R-Really?

07:34.460 --> 07:37.230
Don't fake a surprised look for no reason.

07:37.930 --> 07:39.830
I see. In other words, Haré...

07:42.870 --> 07:45.000
I love you, Weda-san.

07:45.640 --> 07:47.230
No, you shouldn't.

07:47.710 --> 07:52.510
A boy with a promising future like you
shouldn't date an old hag like me.

07:52.850 --> 07:54.450
You want things to turn out this way, huh?

07:54.450 --> 07:57.420
That doesn't even contain
1% of what I'm wishing for.?

07:57.990 --> 07:59.420
You don't mind an old hag?

07:59.660 --> 08:01.680
I don't mind an old hag.

08:02.020 --> 08:03.120
Robert...

08:03.360 --> 08:04.020
Weda.

08:04.790 --> 08:06.850
I think it's totally okay!

08:06.930 --> 08:08.360
A surprise ending!

08:08.430 --> 08:10.900
And I'm telling you, that's wrong!

08:11.300 --> 08:13.560
I just don't like her being hated.

08:13.640 --> 08:15.500
Mom does have good points.

08:15.570 --> 08:16.330
For example?

08:17.270 --> 08:18.170
A good quality.

08:18.570 --> 08:19.730
A good quality.

08:20.140 --> 08:21.340
A good quality.

08:21.540 --> 08:22.440
A good quality...

08:22.610 --> 08:23.700
A good quality...

08:24.010 --> 08:24.780
A good quality...

08:25.280 --> 08:26.180
A good quality...

08:26.620 --> 08:27.840
A good quality...

08:28.520 --> 08:31.080
A good quality of mine?

08:31.290 --> 08:31.880
Yeah.

08:32.320 --> 08:35.810
I just wanted Robert to know
what your good points were.

08:36.860 --> 08:38.220
Let's see...

08:38.360 --> 08:41.520
If I had to give an example, it would be that I
do things at my pace?

08:41.700 --> 08:43.490
In this case, I think that would be a bad trait.

08:43.800 --> 08:48.070
Robert looks up to people who possess
traits that are more amazing than his own.

08:48.240 --> 08:49.670
Yeah, that's it!

08:49.940 --> 08:52.100
Mom, don't you have something amazing?

08:52.210 --> 08:53.770
I'm amazing when I take my clothes off!

08:54.080 --> 08:55.070
Stop that.

08:56.080 --> 08:56.810
Why?

08:56.880 --> 08:57.740
I've seen enough of it.

09:03.190 --> 09:06.050
What are Mom's special traits?

09:06.320 --> 09:09.120
Maybe it is hunting after all...

09:09.690 --> 09:12.220
But what can you hunt here?

09:12.660 --> 09:13.890
Mom is...

09:14.300 --> 09:20.400
...selfish, drunk, lazy, troublesome,
unmotivated, clingy, whiny, forgetful, sleepy,
loves stripping...

09:21.070 --> 09:23.660
I think of her this way and I'm her son!

09:23.970 --> 09:27.310
There's no way that
Robert would come to like Mom...

09:30.010 --> 09:34.110
Hey, Guu, do you know
what Mom's good qualities are?

09:40.290 --> 09:41.850
Weda's strong points?

09:42.160 --> 09:44.020
How she's honest to herself?

09:44.490 --> 09:47.630
Right! That's stretching it a bit,
but that's a good...

09:47.630 --> 09:49.360
She sleeps when she wants to sleep.

09:49.770 --> 09:51.560
She eats when she wants to eat.

09:52.170 --> 09:54.360
She doesn't do anything
that she doesn't want to do.

09:54.540 --> 09:55.270
No good.

09:55.910 --> 10:00.500
If you want them to be friendly that much,
then how about leaving them alone together?

10:01.910 --> 10:03.340
All alone, huh...

10:03.680 --> 10:04.450
Exactly.

10:04.450 --> 10:08.320
If they can sit down and talk things out, he'll
probably think that Weda is a pretty good
person after all.

10:08.680 --> 10:09.410
That's true.

10:09.550 --> 10:11.090
He doesn't have to admire her.

10:11.090 --> 10:13.020
If only he doesn't hate her...

10:13.420 --> 10:14.220
That's right.

10:14.390 --> 10:20.020
He doesn't necessarily have to see
something amazing about mom, like when
she's doing her best at something.

10:20.130 --> 10:21.290
In this case, something less will do.

10:21.430 --> 10:24.190
I see, Weda doing her best...

10:24.930 --> 10:26.990
For now, let's have them be alone for a while.

10:30.240 --> 10:31.540
Then, let's go in here.

10:31.610 --> 10:32.300
All right.

10:32.810 --> 10:35.740
There's one thing that would make Weda do
her best.

10:36.080 --> 10:36.940
What? What is it?

10:37.110 --> 10:41.450
Something that Weda, as a mother,
absolutely would do her best at...

10:41.520 --> 10:42.980
There's only one thing.

10:45.890 --> 10:48.050
Well, bluntly put...

10:48.920 --> 10:51.220
Who's the guy interrupting our game?

10:51.860 --> 10:54.200
Hey, I'm tellin' ya, hurry up
and fill the bags with money!

10:54.200 --> 10:55.030
Y-Yes...

10:55.100 --> 10:56.530
Her son in danger.

10:58.370 --> 11:00.490
Don't make noise, kid!

11:02.570 --> 11:05.060
Hey, who pushed the emergency button?

11:05.310 --> 11:08.610
The hero's party is currently
gathering up their coins.

11:09.110 --> 11:10.980
Dick, cast a protective spell.

11:11.050 --> 11:11.510
Sure.

11:12.620 --> 11:13.910
Magic Shield!

11:15.120 --> 11:16.350
We said, don't make noise!

11:18.520 --> 11:20.750
Now we can see Weda do her best.

11:21.090 --> 11:22.180
Isn't that great, Haré?

11:22.260 --> 11:23.560
It's not great!

11:25.190 --> 11:27.160
It's a bank robbery!

11:29.730 --> 11:32.330
Oh, I wonder if it's a movie shoot.

11:35.200 --> 11:37.140
M-M-M-M-Mom!

11:37.210 --> 11:38.330
Help us!

11:38.710 --> 11:39.610
Stay still!

11:39.810 --> 11:41.040
I'll hit you with a Drain spell!

11:41.210 --> 11:42.840
Can you settle for
something like Poison instead?

11:42.910 --> 11:43.500
Haré!

11:43.910 --> 11:44.710
Guu-sama!

11:44.950 --> 11:47.480
To the robbers,
stop this futile resistance and...

11:47.480 --> 11:49.140
Shut up, you're only a weakling!

11:49.250 --> 11:50.740
Give us money and a car!

11:50.850 --> 11:52.880
We've got hostages!

11:54.260 --> 11:55.090
Weda-san!

11:55.090 --> 11:56.460
Wait here!

11:56.630 --> 11:57.730
I'll go rescue them!

11:57.730 --> 11:58.890
I have to go rescue them.
I'll go rescue them!

12:00.430 --> 12:01.950
What are you thinking?

12:02.260 --> 12:03.990
What? I'm going to go rescue them!

12:04.130 --> 12:05.760
That's my job!

12:05.940 --> 12:08.030
Weda-san, stay here and sit still!

12:08.370 --> 12:09.030
You're kidding me!

12:09.110 --> 12:10.770
I'm going to go rescue Haré!

12:10.910 --> 12:11.740
You can't!

12:11.970 --> 12:13.810
Let go of my hand! That's an order!

12:14.940 --> 12:19.900
I hate how you act so selfishly
and don't think about the
people around you, Weda-san!

12:22.320 --> 12:23.790
I'm supposed to be the
one protecting Haré-sama!

12:23.790 --> 12:24.380
I am!

12:24.490 --> 12:24.890
I am!

12:24.890 --> 12:25.350
ME!
I am!

12:25.490 --> 12:30.430
The first Wacky Haré Rescue Race begins!

12:32.190 --> 12:34.660
Hey, Guu, aren't you scared?

12:36.070 --> 12:36.960
Of what?

12:37.030 --> 12:40.130
I mean... aren't you scared of this situation.

12:42.610 --> 12:43.440
Of that?

12:45.980 --> 12:47.200
Not that...

12:47.280 --> 12:50.710
It was my mistake to expect a human
response out of her.

12:51.610 --> 12:54.520
Maybe I'm just going to die here.

12:54.620 --> 12:55.950
Cheer up.

12:56.350 --> 12:57.220
Guu...

12:58.990 --> 13:01.620
There are plenty of things
tougher than this out there.

13:01.690 --> 13:02.710
I can't take them if there are.

13:02.990 --> 13:05.620
There are many things
that are tougher than death itself.

13:06.030 --> 13:07.690
The only one I really love is you, he said.

13:07.800 --> 13:10.130
I want you to wait for me, he said. I will
definitely return, he said.

13:10.230 --> 13:11.820
He always said things
that were fitting at the time...

13:11.930 --> 13:13.700
That perverted old geezer!

13:13.800 --> 13:14.860
Don't come out at a time like this!

13:14.940 --> 13:16.400
Think about the situation!

13:16.470 --> 13:17.800
You there! Don't move!

13:18.040 --> 13:19.410
S-Sure!

13:19.880 --> 13:22.740
Existence of many tough situations,
example 1.

13:22.880 --> 13:24.900
It doesn't do me much good to know that
right now.

13:26.150 --> 13:28.240
It was such a short life...

13:28.680 --> 13:31.410
A good thing about you, Haré, is that you're
good at resigning yourself.

13:32.020 --> 13:34.620
It was a life that forced me to do so often.

13:35.690 --> 13:37.180
It was fulfilling, then?

13:38.090 --> 13:39.150
I guess so...

13:39.600 --> 13:42.090
It was a life that had its own kind of
happiness.

13:42.630 --> 13:44.000
Happiness...

13:45.500 --> 13:48.200
Happiness! Happiness! Happiness!

13:48.200 --> 13:50.200
I don't want to die yet!

13:50.610 --> 13:51.470
What is it!?

13:51.570 --> 13:52.610
U-Um, well, uh...

13:52.610 --> 13:54.100
Bathroom... I guess?

13:54.440 --> 13:56.410
Hold it. I'm going first.

13:56.880 --> 13:57.740
Okay!

14:05.250 --> 14:06.260
That's where...

14:06.260 --> 14:07.240
I can get in.
I can get in.

14:08.260 --> 14:10.250
I told you to not come with me!

14:10.330 --> 14:11.590
And don't mimic me!

14:11.730 --> 14:12.890
I'm not mimicking you!

14:12.960 --> 14:13.900
Go over there!

14:13.900 --> 14:14.690
I don't want to!

14:15.130 --> 14:15.930
You over there.

14:16.670 --> 14:18.260
This area is off limits.

14:18.870 --> 14:20.460
Please evacuate immediately.

14:23.110 --> 14:24.440
Oh, I'm having one of my seizures!

14:25.840 --> 14:27.470
Are you all right, young lady?

14:27.840 --> 14:29.900
Excuse me, can you call a doctor?

14:30.510 --> 14:32.210
Time is critical! Please hurry!

14:32.310 --> 14:33.280
Uh, sure...

14:33.550 --> 14:34.710
Let's see...

14:35.150 --> 14:37.240
A doctor... a doctor, you say...

14:42.160 --> 14:43.320
Must be working too hard...

14:43.930 --> 14:44.530
Oh, no!

14:44.530 --> 14:45.590
This is tight!

14:45.590 --> 14:46.420
Don't make so much noise!
This is tight!

14:46.600 --> 14:48.030
What are we going to do if they find us!?

14:48.030 --> 14:49.200
You're the noisy one!

14:49.200 --> 14:50.390
Who is!?

14:53.970 --> 14:54.970
Geez, this is taking things too far!

14:54.970 --> 14:56.300
You are, Weda-san!

14:57.470 --> 14:59.870
In any case, they'll find
us easily if we stay here.

14:59.980 --> 15:00.700
Let's hide.

15:00.840 --> 15:02.440
Can you stop ordering me around?

15:02.610 --> 15:03.940
It's not an order!

15:04.010 --> 15:05.570
I'm saying so because it's dangerous!

15:11.850 --> 15:12.840
E-Excuse me...

15:12.920 --> 15:14.250
Please, take your time.

15:20.360 --> 15:22.460
Um, are you a criminal?

15:40.680 --> 15:42.650
That idiot's taking his time pissing...

15:43.220 --> 15:45.550
He better not be boosting his stats by
himself.

15:46.060 --> 15:48.250
Guu, can't you do something?

15:48.460 --> 15:49.450
For example?

15:49.630 --> 15:51.920
You know, like asking them nicely with that
business look of yours.

15:52.060 --> 15:53.260
Business look?

15:55.260 --> 15:56.930
Yeah, that look, that one.

15:57.130 --> 16:00.590
Ask them if they can at least release the
women, children, and the elderly.

16:00.700 --> 16:01.030
Right?

16:01.770 --> 16:02.530
But...

16:02.610 --> 16:04.160
Don't do meaningless things!

16:04.240 --> 16:05.240
You can do it, Guu!

16:05.240 --> 16:06.230
Come on, please?

16:06.440 --> 16:08.140
All right, Guu will do her best.

16:08.210 --> 16:09.270
Oh, oomph!

16:09.510 --> 16:10.880
No need for oomphs!

16:17.290 --> 16:19.950
Don't just sit there, hurry up and release the
hostages, idiot.

16:20.060 --> 16:21.250
Wrong!!

16:21.320 --> 16:23.620
That's what that boy over there was saying!

16:25.060 --> 16:25.790
Oh, that's an amusing thing to say.

16:25.790 --> 16:27.730
I didn't say it, I didn't say it, I didn't say it...
Oh, that's an amusing thing to say.

16:27.730 --> 16:28.330
I didn't say it, I didn't say it, I didn't say it...

16:28.330 --> 16:30.470
I didn't say it, I didn't say it, I didn't say it...
Your face tells me you're quite low level...

16:30.470 --> 16:32.230
I didn't say it, I didn't say it, I didn't say it...

16:36.070 --> 16:38.510
Um, d-d-d-do you like games?

16:39.240 --> 16:41.900
No, no, no, no, it was nothing. Excuse me.

16:42.040 --> 16:42.910
Don't mock me!

16:43.550 --> 16:45.450
Of course I do!

16:47.450 --> 16:51.440
I'm in the middle of raising a monster for the
upcoming tournament.

16:51.820 --> 16:53.340
You know what Pachimon is?

16:53.490 --> 16:55.690
Oh, you mean Pachinko Monsters...

16:55.690 --> 16:58.460
I actually analyze data every so often.

16:58.560 --> 16:59.120
Wanna see?

16:59.400 --> 16:59.790
S-Sure!

17:00.800 --> 17:04.250
I heard that there's a rare monster called
Nagoya-ucchie...

17:04.370 --> 17:06.630
But I don't know where to get it.

17:07.040 --> 17:07.930
Do you know where?

17:08.040 --> 17:10.630
If it's Nagoya-ucchie, I know where it is.

17:10.910 --> 17:12.430
Seriously? Where? Where?

17:12.810 --> 17:15.400
Let's see, it was in the hidden dungeon...

17:15.510 --> 17:17.100
T-The money is ready.

17:17.180 --> 17:17.800
All right! Okay!

17:18.450 --> 17:24.150
Now, to clear this game, I've got the golden
coins, Excalibur...

17:24.650 --> 17:27.280
...the hero's sword, and for last,
the divine shield.

17:29.320 --> 17:30.920
Who should it be?

17:31.530 --> 17:35.590
I hope it's not me. I hope it's not me.
I hope it's not me...

17:36.000 --> 17:37.690
I don't want to go home tonight.

17:37.900 --> 17:39.560
What!?

17:39.700 --> 17:41.000
I want to see the ocean.

17:41.100 --> 17:42.340
Don't ask for the impossible!

17:42.340 --> 17:44.240
If you ask that much...

17:44.610 --> 17:47.270
Oh, and you too, my Pachimon friend.

17:47.480 --> 17:49.340
Friend? Since when?

17:49.550 --> 17:50.840
What are you giving him suggestions?

17:51.580 --> 17:53.840
"Gather roses while you may."

17:53.980 --> 17:54.850
I don't need them!

17:54.850 --> 17:56.450
"Spare the rod and spoil the child."

17:56.450 --> 17:58.940
We might never come back again!

17:59.020 --> 18:01.220
Gimme a break! I can't take it anymore!

18:01.220 --> 18:02.090
Um...

18:03.260 --> 18:04.160
Who's there!?

18:04.830 --> 18:08.000
I-I was upstairs, and didn't
realize what was going on...

18:08.000 --> 18:11.300
...and a guy in a hat told
me to come downstairs...

18:11.530 --> 18:13.930
Mom, what's with that falsetto?

18:14.070 --> 18:16.090
No, wait, why are you here!?

18:16.810 --> 18:17.930
Where's the guy with the hat?

18:18.140 --> 18:21.370
He said he was going to
see if anyone else was around.

18:24.310 --> 18:26.680
It looks like the gang leader is the guy
downstairs.

18:26.950 --> 18:28.810
I'll be the decoy.

18:29.790 --> 18:31.090
It's all right.

18:31.090 --> 18:32.080
I'm good at it.

18:32.250 --> 18:34.810
Besides, Robert, you're tough...

18:35.490 --> 18:37.190
I have to settle this in one shot.

18:37.790 --> 18:40.460
For Haré-sama... and Weda-san.

18:41.560 --> 18:42.530
Go over there.

18:44.370 --> 18:45.200
What should I do?

18:45.200 --> 18:46.790
Haré is too close to the robber!

18:47.400 --> 18:48.270
Hurry up!

18:49.540 --> 18:50.730
Wait, Robert!

18:57.950 --> 18:59.740
I'll take that item.

19:00.120 --> 19:02.740
Otherwise, you'll see a bad ending.

19:08.260 --> 19:10.450
You're disturbing my important game.

19:11.130 --> 19:13.960
Well, maybe this is one of the events to go
through.

19:15.030 --> 19:20.660
I guess I'll defeat one of the bosses and get
bonus points.

19:21.200 --> 19:23.030
After all, it's our turn next.

19:29.610 --> 19:30.340
See ya!

19:45.360 --> 19:45.950
Dammit!

19:46.660 --> 19:49.500
Game over, so to say...

19:51.570 --> 19:52.970
A bad end, huh...

19:55.940 --> 19:58.630
Mom! I was so scared!

19:58.710 --> 20:01.610
It's all right, you're fine, I'm glad...

20:01.680 --> 20:02.340
Hey!

20:03.080 --> 20:04.440
Pachimon kid...

20:04.680 --> 20:07.310
I forgot to ask you
where the rare monster lives.

20:07.780 --> 20:09.510
Oh, that's...

20:09.720 --> 20:11.450
No, you don't have to tell me...

20:11.590 --> 20:14.610
Since it looks like I'll have plenty of free time
coming up.

20:17.230 --> 20:20.530
It was an incident that happened because
someone confused a game with reality.

20:21.300 --> 20:22.560
Don't act so political...

20:22.560 --> 20:24.030
Is that how you're going to wrap this up?

20:26.670 --> 20:28.830
Ah, paradise...

20:28.900 --> 20:32.970
Geez, just when Robert started to think
better of you...

20:33.680 --> 20:37.440
If he sees you like this, his evaluation of you
will go down again.

20:37.880 --> 20:39.400
So this is where you were.

20:39.720 --> 20:41.240
T-That's not it, Robert!

20:41.320 --> 20:43.150
Well, this Mom we have here is a fake...

20:43.250 --> 20:45.740
That's right! She's controlled
by the evil syndicate, and...

20:45.850 --> 20:45.890
...and this really isn't how she is...

20:45.890 --> 20:47.660
What's this about a syndicate?
...and this really isn't how she is...

20:47.660 --> 20:48.120
...and this really isn't how she is...

20:48.260 --> 20:49.450
I know that.

20:49.520 --> 20:51.720
Haré-sama, you saw through it all along.

20:52.790 --> 20:56.230
...that how Weda-san
usually lives is all an act!

20:56.930 --> 20:57.490
Huh?

20:58.230 --> 21:04.370
She usually acts careless and lazy to fool
people and catch them off guard!

21:04.440 --> 21:07.070
Ah, that's right. Yeah, that's it exactly.

21:07.680 --> 21:09.270
You're so awesome, Weda-san!

21:09.410 --> 21:12.310
More than that, I'm thirsty.

21:12.610 --> 21:15.340
I want to drink a frothy drink
that's similar to barley tea.

21:15.520 --> 21:17.140
You're going to pretend to drink beer!

21:17.290 --> 21:18.120
Yes, sir!

21:21.820 --> 21:24.310
Another servant friend.

22:33.360 --> 22:34.490
NEXT EPISODE

22:35.090 --> 22:37.390
This is an adult's love story.

22:37.390 --> 22:40.500
An unexpected reunion of Weda and Clive in the city.

22:40.500 --> 22:44.130
Where will the two head, their hearts trembling from premonitions of a
passionate romance?

22:44.130 --> 22:46.600
Now, now, now, that's slightly different!

22:46.600 --> 22:49.400
We're going to rescue Mom from the evil
clutches of the school doc!

22:49.400 --> 22:50.940
Come on! Hurry up, we're going
to follow him.

22:50.940 --> 22:52.940
Geez, we're going to lose sight of him!

22:52.940 --> 22:57.110
Well, damn him! Of all places to
take Mom to, he took here there!?

22:57.450 --> 22:58.150
Next episode of Haré+Guu: "Rest Stop"

22:58.150 --> 23:00.980
Next episode of Haré+Guu: "Rest Stop"

23:00.980 --> 23:02.720
By the way, Haré doesn't wear underwear.

23:02.720 --> 23:03.550
Of course she's wrong!
